# provenance: the TrapStateSnapshot consumption step (EntityEventSync.cs:99-116)
# — the late-joiner one-shot consumption was LOG-ONLY until the phase-5 fix
# (2026-08-12): a late joiner entering the world must replay every consumed
# one-shot entity against its regenerated world (the registry's facts,
# TrapConsumptionRegistry.SendSnapshot). Two entities consumed; the snapshot
# arrives; the late joiner replays both (the relays from the triggering frame
# already consumed the per-entity guard once — the snapshot entries are
# dropped as duplicates, which is exactly the idempotency the design relies
# on); the 60 s re-send (WorldEventSync's cycle) must NOT re-consume.
# Mechanism: TrapStateSnapshotMsg (NetMsg 67), the per-entity replay guard.
@0 event g1 MineExploded 10 20
@0 event g1 BioTerminalUnlocked 30 40
@33 expect executed MineExploded 1 within 500
@33 expect executed BioTerminalUnlocked 1 within 500
@33 snapshot g2
@66 expect replayed g2 MineExploded 1 within 500
@66 expect replayed g2 BioTerminalUnlocked 1 within 500
@66 snapshot g2
@99 expect replayed g2 MineExploded 1 within 500
@99 expect replayed g2 BioTerminalUnlocked 1 within 500
